<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        clipi runs with the hardened runtime (Developer ID + notarization
        require it), but doesn't need any of the runtime-relaxing entitlements:
        no JIT, no unsigned dylibs, no disabled library validation. The features
        we use (Carbon hot key, NSPasteboard, AX, CGEvent.post) all work under
        bare hardened runtime — Accessibility is a separate user-granted
        permission, not an entitlement.

        Leaving the dict empty is intentional: it produces a hardened-runtime
        binary with no scope to reduce, which gives notarization the cleanest
        possible review and avoids accidentally weakening the app's posture.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
